course: dictionary
lesson: 5242
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around a word are its context, and they show you which meaning the writer wants. «A good way to do a jigsaw is to find the edges and corners first.» Here jigsaw means a picture cut into pieces, because you find edge pieces to make a frame.
explain: Now read this: «Look at a world map and slide South America over to Africa: the bulge of Brazil tucks into the curve of West Africa like two jigsaw pieces.» Brazil and Africa are not a saw or a tool here. The word means puzzle pieces that fit together.
explain: Sometimes the meaning is a comparison. In a story, a detective fits clues together «like a jigsaw». The detective is not cutting wood, so jigsaw means a hard problem with many parts that must be fitted together. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Jigsaw» can mean a picture cut into many oddly shaped pieces that you fit together, as in «jigsaw puzzle».
fact: «Jigsaw» can also mean a saw with a thin blade for cutting curves in wood.
fact: «Jigsaw» can mean a difficult problem with many parts that must be fitted together.
fact: A 100-piece jigsaw has 100 pieces, and the last piece of the jigsaw is the one that finishes the picture.
exercise: «A good way to do a jigsaw is to find the edges and corners first.» What is a jigsaw in this sentence? | A pair of scissors | A saw with a thin blade | *A picture cut into pieces that you fit together | A kind of bridge
exercise: In design technology, Sam uses a jigsaw with an adult to cut a curve in wood. What is a jigsaw here? | *A saw with a thin blade for cutting curves in wood | A hard problem with many parts | A small hammer | A puzzle with many pieces
exercise: «The coasts of South America and Africa fit together like jigsaw pieces.» What does this suggest? | Parts that float away | Parts that will never meet | *Parts that match exactly, like the pieces of a puzzle | Parts that are all the same colour
test: «Brazil tucks into West Africa like two jigsaw pieces.» What does jigsaw mean in this sentence? | A saw for cutting wood | A kind of map drawn on paper | A game played with cards | *Puzzle pieces that fit together
test: The detective fits the clues together like a jigsaw. What does jigsaw mean here? | A picture of a map | *A hard problem with many parts to fit together | A kind of game with cards | A saw for cutting wood
exam: Which word means a picture cut into oddly shaped pieces that you fit together? | *Jigsaw | Blade | Edge | Saw
